<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45090" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spŏlĭātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		spolio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a pillaging</i>, <i>robbing</i>, <i>plundering</i>, <i>spoliation</i>
			(class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in tantā spoliatione omnium rerum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Sest. 21, 47</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sacrorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					29, 8, 9</span></i>
			.— <i>Plur.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spoliationes fanorum atque oppidorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 4, 59, § 132</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Agr. 1, 3, 9</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">consulatūs,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Mur. 40, 87</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dignitatis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Phil. 2, 11, 27</span></i>
			.</div>
